      "title": "24.4 Alkanenitriles (–CN group wale compounds) (Roman Urdu)",
      "language": "roman_ur",
      "variant_of": "C12-CHEM-CH24-24.4",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "2d720c54-503b-58ec-b5b1-3307f222f40c",
          "pdf_from": 127,
          "pdf_to": 127,
          "note": "Roman Urdu explanation of topic 24.4 (PDF 127)."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Jin organic compounds mein -CN functional group ho unhein alkanenitriles kehte hain. Maslan:"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\underset{\\text{ethanenitrile}}{\\ce{CH3-CN}} \\qquad \\underset{\\text{propanenitrile}}{\\ce{CH3-CH2-CN}}",
            "text_alt": "CH₃–CN (ethanenitrile)    CH₃–CH₂–CN (propanenitrile)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Alkanenitriles banane ka tareeqa chapter 21 mein diya ja chuka hai (halogenoalkane + KCN)."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Alkanenitriles bohat se chemical reactions mein important (ahem) hain, lekin in ka sab se important use hydrolysis (paani se torna) ke zariye carboxylic acids banana hai. Nitriles ki hydrolysis dilute (halke) acid aur dilute alkali, dono se ho sakti hai."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
